WEBVTT

1
00:00:12.211 --> 00:00:16.094
mild October evening, Anne leaned back in her chair and sighed.

2
00:00:17.055 --> 00:00:20.517
She was sitting at a table covered with textbooks and exercises.

3
00:00:22.198 --> 00:00:22.819
"What is the matter?"

4
00:00:23.199 --> 00:00:24.980
asked Gilbert, who had just arrived.

5
00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.401
"How's school going?

6
00:00:27.482 --> 00:00:30.284
I heard you are doing a splendid job and all the children like you."

7
00:00:31.808 --> 00:00:35.071
"Actually, no, not all," said Anne.

8
00:00:35.091 --> 00:00:39.074
"Anthony Pye doesn't and won't like me.

9
00:00:40.235 --> 00:00:42.297
And what's worse is he doesn't respect me.

10
00:00:42.817 --> 00:00:46.000
I don't mind confessing to you that it worries me miserably.

11
00:00:46.560 --> 00:00:51.484
I've tried every way to win him over, and I'm beginning to fear I never shall.

12
00:00:52.205 --> 00:00:54.707
But we'll see what patience and kindness can do."

13
00:00:54.727 --> 00:00:57.570
"Do you at least like teaching?"

14
00:00:57.970 --> 00:00:58.690
asked Gilbert.

15
00:00:58.710 --> 00:01:00.292
"I do.

16
00:01:01.940 --> 00:01:05.163
Why, I've learned more in the past few weeks of teaching than in all the years I went

17
00:01:05.203 --> 00:01:06.043
to school myself!"

18
00:01:07.845 --> 00:01:12.708
Anne and Gilbert talked for a while about their plans, and Gilbert announced that he wanted to study

19
00:01:12.768 --> 00:01:13.589
to be a doctor.

20
00:01:13.609 --> 00:01:18.032
"I want to do my share of honest, real work in the world, Anne."

21
00:01:20.254 --> 00:01:23.776
"I'd like to add some beauty to life," said Anne dreamily.

22
00:01:23.796 --> 00:01:32.069
"I don't exactly want to make people know more—though I know that teaching is the noblest ambition— but

23
00:01:32.129 --> 00:01:36.291
I'd love for people to have some little joy or happy thought because of me."

24
00:01:36.311 --> 00:01:42.194
"I think you're fulfilling that ambition every day," said Gilbert admiringly.

25
00:01:44.294 --> 00:01:49.417
Gilbert left, and when Marilla returned home, the fire was crackling and Anne had dinner ready.

26
00:01:50.797 --> 00:01:53.118
But Marilla sank wearily into her chair.

27
00:01:53.138 --> 00:01:55.759
"Are your eyes troubling you?

28
00:01:56.399 --> 00:01:57.672
Does your head ache?"

29
00:01:57.692 --> 00:01:59.053
queried Anne anxiously.

30
00:01:59.073 --> 00:02:01.454
"No," said Marilla.

31
00:02:01.474 --> 00:02:06.256
"I'm just tired and worried about my cousin Mary and her children.

32
00:02:07.016 --> 00:02:09.577
Mary is very ill and may die soon."

33
00:02:09.597 --> 00:02:12.118
"What are the children like?

34
00:02:12.798 --> 00:02:13.539
How old are they?"

35
00:02:13.939 --> 00:02:14.539
Anne asked.

36
00:02:15.679 --> 00:02:19.461
"They're twins—six years old," replied Marilla.

37
00:02:19.481 --> 00:02:24.003
"Oh, I've always been especially interested in twins since Mrs.

38
00:02:24.043 --> 00:02:26.624
Hammond had so many," said Anne eagerly.

39
00:02:28.288 --> 00:02:29.028
"Are they pretty?"

40
00:02:29.048 --> 00:02:32.250
"Goodness, I couldn't tell," said Marilla.

41
00:02:32.270 --> 00:02:34.611
"They were too dirty.

42
00:02:35.191 --> 00:02:39.412
Davy was making mud pies outside, and he pushed Dora into the mud.

43
00:02:40.733 --> 00:02:45.435
Mary said Dora was really a very good child but that Davy was full of mischief."

44
00:02:46.735 --> 00:02:48.256
Marilla paused for a moment.

45
00:02:48.276 --> 00:02:52.478
"Anne, I'm sure Mary wants me to take those children.

46
00:02:53.158 --> 00:02:55.939
She didn't say so, but I'm sure she thinks it."

47
00:02:55.959 --> 00:03:00.285
"Oh!" Anne clasped her hands with excitement.

48
00:03:00.305 --> 00:03:03.665
"And of course you will, Marilla, won't you?"

49
00:03:03.685 --> 00:03:07.847
"I haven't made up my mind," said Marilla.

50
00:03:09.207 --> 00:03:14.208
Marilla thought there was only one thing you could say about twins: they were twice as bad as

51
00:03:14.248 --> 00:03:15.229
a single child.

52
00:03:15.249 --> 00:03:20.530
"I think twins are very interesting," repeated Anne.

53
00:03:20.550 --> 00:03:22.931
"At least one pair of them."

54
00:03:24.091 --> 00:03:32.579
Marilla frowned and said, "Dora seems good and quiet, but that Davy Anne was fond of children, and

55
00:03:32.619 --> 00:03:37.623
the memory of her own lonely childhood before she came to Green Gables was still very vivid.

56
00:03:37.643 --> 00:03:42.666
"It's our duty to look after them, Marilla," Anne insisted.

57
00:03:42.686 --> 00:03:47.470
"I suppose it is," Marilla agreed with some reluctance.

58
00:03:47.490 --> 00:03:50.592
"Don't look so happy, Anne.

59
00:03:50.932 --> 00:03:52.573
It will mean extra work for you.

60
00:03:53.274 --> 00:03:56.256
My eyes are bad, so you'll have to make their clothes.

61
00:03:57.172 --> 00:03:58.533
And you don't like sewing."

62
00:04:00.714 --> 00:04:06.478
"I do hate sewing," said Anne calmly, "but it's good for people to do things they don't like

63
00:04:06.958 --> 00:04:07.818
in moderation."

64
00:04:09.139 --> 00:04:10.820
A few weeks later, Mrs.

65
00:04:10.900 --> 00:04:13.202
Lynde was sitting at her kitchen window, knitting.

66
00:04:14.102 --> 00:04:16.043
Five years previously, Mrs.

67
00:04:16.123 --> 00:04:21.867
Lynde had sat at the same window and watched Matthew Cuthbert drive past with Anne when the young

68
00:04:21.927 --> 00:04:23.688
girl first arrived in Avonlea.

69
00:04:25.332 --> 00:04:29.333
"There's Marilla coming home from her cousin's funeral," Mrs.

70
00:04:29.393 --> 00:04:32.754
Lynde said to her husband, "and she's got the twins with her.

71
00:04:34.315 --> 00:04:39.076
Yes, there's Davy trying to grab the pony's tail and Marilla jerking him back.

72
00:04:41.557 --> 00:04:43.237
Dora's sitting up straight.

73
00:04:44.077 --> 00:04:46.858
She always looks as if she's just been starched and ironed."

74
00:04:48.439 --> 00:04:52.740
The pony jogged past the Lyndes' farm and along the lane to Green Gables.

75
00:04:54.068 --> 00:04:55.749
Marilla's face was rather grim.

76
00:04:56.910 --> 00:05:01.653
She could not make Davy sit still and worried that he might fall off the buggy and break

77
00:05:01.693 --> 00:05:02.193
his neck.

78
00:05:03.234 --> 00:05:05.855
In despair she finally threatened to smack him.

79
00:05:06.956 --> 00:05:13.180
Whereupon Davy climbed into her lap, flung his chubby arms about her neck, and gave her a bear-like

80
00:05:13.200 --> 00:05:19.564
hug. "I don't believe you mean it," Davy said, touching her wrinkled cheek affectionately.

81
00:05:21.068 --> 00:05:23.789
"You don't look like a lady who'd smack a little boy.

82
00:05:24.410 --> 00:05:26.831
Didn't you find it hard to keep still when you were little?"

83
00:05:26.851 --> 00:05:35.155
"No, I always kept still when I was told," said Marilla, trying to speak sternly but warming to

84
00:05:35.215 --> 00:05:35.955
Davy's hugs.

85
00:05:37.276 --> 00:05:41.018
"Well, I suppose that was because you're a girl," said Davy.

86
00:05:41.038 --> 00:05:43.499
"Dora can sit still.

87
00:05:44.039 --> 00:05:45.040
But it's not as fun."

88
00:05:46.536 --> 00:05:50.959
"How can you be such a naughty boy when your poor mother's funeral was today?"

89
00:05:51.419 --> 00:05:53.220
demanded Marilla despairingly.

90
00:05:53.240 --> 00:05:58.102
"But she was glad to die," said Davy confidentially.

91
00:05:58.122 --> 00:06:00.504
"I know, because she told me so.

92
00:06:02.105 --> 00:06:03.565
Mother was tired of being sick.

93
00:06:04.946 --> 00:06:07.007
We had a long talk before she died.

94
00:06:07.688 --> 00:06:10.689
She said you would take me and Dora, and I would be a good boy."

95
00:06:12.790 --> 00:06:15.572
They arrived at Green Gables, and Anne greeted them.

96
00:06:16.208 --> 00:06:23.321
Dora calmly allowed herself to be kissed, but Davy gave Anne a hearty hug and cheerfully announced, "I'm

97
00:06:23.381 --> 00:06:24.564
Mr. Davy Keith."
